        "original_id": "a8e84d0f-74f9-5ef7-9c84-ba62a2b96537",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: RedBoot, Airbus A380\n- Organizations: Red Hat, Airbus, Delta Air Lines\n- Systems: eCos real-time operating system, Hardware Abstraction Layer\n- Topics: embedded systems, bootstrap firmware, open source software\n\nFacts:\n- RedBoot is an acronym for Red Hat Embedded Debug and Bootstrap firmware.\n- RedBoot is an open source application.\n- RedBoot uses the eCos real-time operating system Hardware Abstraction Layer to provide bootstrap firmware for embedded systems.\n- RedBoot is used in product development and in deployed products in the field.\n- RedBoot is used in entertainment systems on Airbus A380 aircraft.\n- RedBoot is used in entertainment systems on Delta Air Lines' Boeing 767 aircraft.\n- The Airbus A380 is a double-deck, wide-body, four-engine jet airliner.\n- Airbus manufactures the Airbus A380.",
